A trough is filled with a liquid of density {eq}825 \; \mathrm{ kg}/ \mathrm{ m}^3

{/eq}. The ends of the trough are equilateral triangles with sides {eq}4 \; \mathrm{ m}

{/eq} long and vertex at the bottom. Find the hydrostatic force on one end of the trough.

Differentiate the function.
{eq}\displaystyle y = \ln (x^8 \sin^2 x)
{/eq}

Balance the following redox reaction occurring in a basic solution.

{eq}\rm ClO^- (aq) + Cr (OH)_4^-(aq) \to CrO_4^{2-} (aq) + Cl^-(aq)

{/eq}

Calculate the iterated integral.

{eq}\int_{0}^{3} \int_{0}^{3} (2x + y)^8 \, \mathrm{d}x \, \mathrm{d}y

{/eq}

Find the general solution to the homogeneous differential equation
{eq}\frac { d ^ { 2 } y } { d t ^ { 2 } } - 16 \frac { d y } { d t } + 164 y = 0.
{/eq}

Which of the following is not expressed in the power unit:
(a) {eq}\text{Energy}=\text{kg}\times \text{m/s} {/eq}
(b) {eq}\text{Pressure}=\text{N/}{{\text{m}}^{2}} {/eq}
(c) {eq}\text{Density}=\text{kg}\times {{\text{m}}^{-3}} {/eq}
(d) {eq}\text{Stress/Strain}=\text{N/}{{\text{m}}^{2}} {/eq}
(e) {eq}\text{Surface tension}=\text{N/m} {/eq}

What is reduced in the following reaction?

{eq}Fe_{2}O_{3} + 3H_{2} \rightarrow 2Fe + 3H_{2}O

{/eq}

A soccer player takes a penalty kick {eq}11.0\ \mathrm{m}

{/eq} from the goal. To score, she has to shoot the ball under the {eq}2.44\ \mathrm{m}

{/eq} high crossbar. If she kicks at {eq}19.8\ \mathrm{m/s}

{/eq}, what range of launch angles will result in a goal?

By using integral testing, can the convergence or divergence of the following series be determined?

{eq}\sum\limits_{n = 1}^{\infty}\frac{cos(n+1)\pi}{n^{3/2}}

{/eq}

Evaluate the indefinite integral.

{eq}\int 23 \cos^2 (23x) dx
{/eq}

There are two identical, positively charged conducting spheres fixed in space. The spheres are 46.0 cm apart (center to center) and repel each other with an electrostatic force of {eq}F_1 = 0.0720 \ \mathrm{N}

{/eq}. Then, a thin conducting wire connects the spheres, redistributing the charge on each sphere. When the wire is removed, the spheres still repel but with a force of {eq}F_2 = 0.100 \ \mathrm{N}

{/eq}. Using this information, find the initial charge on each sphere, {eq}q_1

{/eq} and {eq}q_2

{/eq}, if initially {eq}q_1 < q_2

{/eq}. The Coulomb Force constant is {eq}k = 1/(4 \pi \epsilon_0) = 8.99 \times 10^9 \ \mathrm{Nm^2/C^2}

{/eq}.
